# Copy to .env.local at the repository root, then fill in the two passwords:
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is gitignored and is for local development only. It sits BELOW real
# environment variables in precedence, so it cannot affect CI, which has no such
# file, and it can never outrank a -D flag. It exists for one reason: with it in
# place an IDE gutter run needs no run configuration at all, because nothing has
# to be injected by the build.
#
# Names are the environment-variable form of the configuration keys:
# toolshop.admin.password becomes TOOLSHOP_ADMIN_PASSWORD. Any key from
# docs/CONFIGURATION.md can be set here, not only these two.
#
# The seeded passwords are published in the application under test's own README:
#   https://github.com/testsmith-io/practice-software-testing
# They are still supplied this way rather than committed. A rule that is relaxed
# for the values that do not matter is not in place for the ones that do.

TOOLSHOP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
TOOLSHOP_CUSTOMER_PASSWORD=
